# Lanternlight - ignore rules
#
# Two jobs: keep build/tool noise out, and keep operator PII out. The second
# job is the one that actually matters - see the PII HAZARD block below.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Scratch / working dirs - never part of the published tree
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
scratchpad/
_scratch/
scratch/
tmp/
.tmp/
ops/runtime/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captures, frames and screenshots
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
frames/
captures/
capture/
screenshots/
frames/**
captures/**
capture/**
screenshots/**
frames/*.png
captures/*.png
capture/*.png
screenshots/*.png
frames/*.jpg
captures/*.jpg
capture/*.jpg
screenshots/*.jpg
frames/*.jpeg
captures/*.jpeg
frames/*.webp
captures/*.webp
frames/*.mp4
captures/*.mp4


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Guard probes - throwaway evidence a running test plants at the repo ROOT
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# tests/_tracked.py's probe_path() writes these to prove the hygiene guards
# are not vacuous. They must be planted at the real root, because scanning the
# real root is the point of the guards. Ignoring them here is what makes a
# CONCURRENT suite safe: it removes them from every
# `git ls-files --others --exclude-standard` in the repository at once - all
# FOUR sites: tests/_tracked.py, ops/lanes.py, tests/test_lane_state.py and
# tests/test_tracked_walker.py - so no walker can ever see another process's
# probe.
#
# Measured 2026-08-26: five concurrent full suites went red in 9 of 10 runs
# without this. See ROADMAP OPS-8.
#
# tests/_tracked.py adds a process's OWN probes back by name, so a probe is
# still visible to the guard that planted it. Never rely on this rule to hide
# a probe from its owner.
_guard_probe_*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
logs/**
*.log
*.log.[0-9]
*.log.[0-9][0-9]
*.logs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game saves and extracted / derived game data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.sav
*.sav.bak
*.savegame

# An ENCODED copy of a save is the same hazard wearing a different extension,
# and blocking only `*.sav` is what creates the pressure to make one. Measured
# 2026-08-09: the repository's own GVAS fixtures exist as base64 precisely
# because `*.sav` is blocked here. So the encoded forms are blocked too.
*.sav.b64
*.sav.base64
*.sav.hex
*.sav.txt
*.sav.gz
*.sav.zip
*.gvas
*.gvas.b64
*.gvas.base64
*.gvas.hex

# ...with one carve-out. `tests/fixtures/` is where REVIEWED, redacted fixtures
# live, and everything there is content-scanned by `tests/test_no_pii.py`,
# which now decodes base64 and hex rather than being blind to them. A fixture
# that reaches this directory has been through the redactor; a `.gvas.b64`
# anywhere else has not, and that is exactly the distinction the path rule can
# make and a content scan cannot.
!tests/fixtures/**/*.gvas.b64

# The same family for logs. The game log carries the operator's SteamID64,
# persona, platform ids and an IP-resolved location - encoding it changes
# nothing about that.
*.log.b64
*.log.base64
*.log.hex
*.log.gz

data/mhdata/
data/mhdata/**
data/extracted/
data/raw/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and credentials
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
API-Key-*.txt
*api-key*.txt
*apikey*.txt
*.key
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
.env
.env.*
secrets.json
credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent / editor / OS local config
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# .claude/ is DELIBERATELY TRACKED here, unlike in the sibling projects on this
# machine. The governance in it - the session default, the subagent definitions,
# the ASCII and commit gates - is the point of the repo being reproducible. A
# fresh clone that gets CLAUDE.md but not the hooks and agents gets half the
# rules and none of the enforcement. Only genuinely machine-local files are
# excluded below.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/**/local.*
.claude/projects/
.claude/todos/
.claude/statsig/
.claude/shell-snapshots/
.mcp.json
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ===========================================================================
# PII HAZARD - anything copied out of the game's Saved tree
# ===========================================================================
#
# Mistfall Hunter writes a log and save tree under the local application data
# directory (on Windows: %LOCALAPPDATA%\MistfallHunter\Saved\). Those files are
# NOT anonymous. Observed contents include, at minimum:
#
#   - the player's SteamID64
#   - the player's Steam persona name
#   - GSDK openID / userId values
#   - an Epic Online Services ProductUserId
#   - geolocation resolved from the player's public IP address
#
# Any of those, committed once, is public forever - a force-push does not
# unpublish a value someone already cloned or that a mirror already indexed.
#
# RULE: never copy anything out of that tree into the repo working directory.
# If you must inspect a real log, read it in place, outside the repo. If a
# sample is genuinely needed for a test, hand-author a synthetic fixture with
# obviously fake identifiers - do not redact a real one, because redaction is
# a per-field allowlist problem and the next game patch adds a field.
#
# The patterns below are a backstop for when that rule is broken anyway. The
# pre-commit hook in .githooks/ is a second backstop. Neither is the primary
# control; the primary control is not copying the files.
# ===========================================================================
MistfallHunter/
**/MistfallHunter/Saved/
**/Saved/Logs/
**/Saved/SaveGames/
**/Saved/Crashes/
Saved/
*MistfallHunter*.log
*MistfallHunter*.sav
mistfall_saved/
game_logs/
game_saves/
pii/
private/
